# The two env vars this app needs to boot against the local Supabase stack
# (supabase/config.toml). Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored, per
# `.env*` in .gitignore) and fill in real values before running `npm run
# dev` or the test suite.
#
# Whole-branch review Finding I1 (2026-09-07 fix wave): these were
# previously documented in no tracked file — `supabase/.env.example`
# covers only the SERVER-side `SUPABASE_AUTH_*` variables (Google OAuth,
# Twilio), not these two CLIENT-side `VITE_` ones. Without them, `getClient()`
# (src/session/supabase.ts) throws `supabaseUrl is required.`, and a plain
# `git clone && npm install && npm run dev` gave a blank page with no
# diagnostic. `onAuthChange` (src/session/auth.ts) now fails soft — a
# missing/misconfigured value degrades the app to signed-out, local-only
# rather than crashing — but this file is the actual fix for "no diagnostic":
# it exists so a fresh clone has something to copy and fill in.
#
# Values below are the Supabase CLI's own well-known local-dev demo
# constants (the same ones already sitting in this worktree's `.env.local`,
# per that file's own comment) — safe to commit as an EXAMPLE, but never
# commit the real `.env.local` itself regardless.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54331
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0

# C8 "Describe it in your own words" — two more VITE_ vars, both OFF/safe
# by default (src/session/featureFlags.ts). Describe-it ships off: leave
# this file's values as they are and nothing about the feature turns on.
# Uncomment VITE_DESCRIBE_IT to try it locally — the only value that
# enables it is exactly `on`, nothing else (not `true`, not `1`).
# VITE_DESCRIBE_IT=on

# The interpreter that turns a free-text answer into a structured one.
# `sim` needs no key and is the default. Leave this unset (or set to
# `sim`); any value other than exactly `gemini` falls back to `sim`.
# VITE_INTERPRETER=sim

# The real Gemini adapter (Task 18) is wired and registered, but turning
# VITE_INTERPRETER=gemini on for real needs a key of your own from Google
# AI Studio, below — there is no shared/default one, and this line ships
# commented out for a reason beyond "no key yet": Task 18's compliance gate
# (data-use/PII terms for the tier you use) has NOT been verified by
# anyone, for any tier, as of this line being written. Read those terms
# for your own tier before you ever set this for real — see this task's
# report/completion note for the full checklist. A VITE_-prefixed key is
# bundled into the client and extractable by any visitor of a deployed
# build; this is safe ONLY for local-only use against `localhost`, never
# for a deployed build with the flag on (see the task's handoff notes on
# the server-side-proxy requirement for real deployment).
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
